\f2\b\fs40 \cf2 \strokec2 1. The irreversible point in atomic completion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs32 \cf2 The irreversibility point is the single\'a0
\f3\fs28 \cb5 COMMIT
\f1\fs32 \cb3 \'a0of the transaction that contains the receipt write.
\f0 \'a0Everything before it must be either invisible, idempotent, or rolled back; everything after it is pure communication. Three rules make this provable:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Durable bytes always precede commit.
\f0 \'a0Publish each output into the SHA-256 tree (write temp \uc0\u8594  fsync file \u8594  rename to\'a0
\f4\fs28 \cb5 managed/<prefix>/<hash>
\f0\fs32 \cb3 \'a0\uc0\u8594  fsync directory)\'a0
\f5\i before
\f0\i0 \'a0opening\'a0
\f6\fs28 \cb5 BEGIN IMMEDIATE
\f0\fs32 \cb3 . Content addressing makes publication idempotent: renaming onto an existing verified file is a no-op, so dedupe falls out for free.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The receipt is written inside the commit, never after.
\f0 \'a0This is what makes lost-acknowledgment replay return the stored result rather than re-executing.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The database may reference only bytes already durable; the tree may contain only referenced bytes or orphans.
\f0 \'a0Disagreement is permitted in exactly one direction \'97 extra unreferenced bytes \'97 which is invisible and collectible. The reverse (rows pointing at missing bytes) is structurally impossible.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 One refinement to doc 27 \'a74: it lists "managed-media materialization" inside the writer callback. If quarantine and the managed tree share a filesystem, materialization is a rename and cheap enough in-lock; if not, copy outside the lock and rename in-lock. Either way, in-lock work must be O(stat), never O(copy) \'97 writer occupancy is the scarcest resource in the system.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

