\f2\b\fs40 \cf2 \strokec2 2. The smallest slice that disproves the most architecture\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf2 The Phase-A journey is right; make it adversarial. One production-shaped journey \'97\'a0
\f1 t2i \uc0\u8594  gallery row \u8594  place into timeline via editor CAS save \u8594  Remotion render \u8594  Range/ETag playback
\f0 , run with a second editor saving concurrently \'97 crosses every authority boundary and every concurrency seam. Nothing smaller touches the document/CAS/render triangle; anything bigger (orchestrators) tests breadth instead of the risky seams.\
Embed these forced failures, each mapped to the clause it attacks:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f6\fs28 \cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 kill -9
\f0\fs32 \cb3 \'a0worker mid-generation \uc0\u8594  lease expiry \u8594  reclaim \u8594  second attempt succeeds; assert no zombie GPU process holds the model and no duplicate gallery row.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Server commits but the completion response is dropped \uc0\u8594  replay same key \u8594  stored result, exactly once.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Poisoned/truncated/hash-mismatched bytes \uc0\u8594  clean rejection, zero partial authority, capability stays advertised with actionable error.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Disk filled to threshold mid-publication \uc0\u8594  clean failure plus setup guidance.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Concurrent editor save versus completion-time registry merge \uc0\u8594  editor sees a genuine CAS conflict; merge applies against the\'a0
\f5\i new
\f0\i0 \'a0head inside the writer transaction; no clobber. (This is the subtlest seam in the whole system.)\cb1 \
