\f2\b\fs40 \cf2 \strokec2 4. Stable capability contracts over evolving executors\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf2 Three concentric rings, each with its own change discipline:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ring 1 \'97 public and slow:
\f0 \'a0
\f6\fs28 \cb5 \{family, input\}
\f0\fs32 \cb3 \'a0shapes, output policy, media kinds, the five error categories. Explicit\'a0
\f6\fs28 \cb5 contract_version
\f0\fs32 \cb3 . Changes here are product migrations gated by the conformance suite.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ring 2 \'97 capability level:
\f0 \'a0flat IDs with per-capability input validators and output policies. Evolution rule: additive optional fields with defaults are compatible; renaming, removal, or semantic change under the same ID is forbidden \'97 ship a new ID or a reviewed registry revision with drain/restart.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ring 3 \'97 executor-private:
\f0 \'a0WGP internals, patches, Comfy graphs, process ABI. Change freely behind the boot probe and smoke gate.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 The fields that separate compatible change from break, recorded in the boot/build manifest and completion provenance:\'a0
\f6\fs28 \cb5 worker_contract_version
\f0\fs32 \cb3 , per-capability\'a0
\f6\fs28 \cb5 capability_contract_version
\f0\fs32 \cb3 ,\'a0
\f6\fs28 \cb5 spec_schema_version
\f0\fs32 \cb3 , and the executor build manifest (Wan SHA, patchset hash, node/template digests). The deciding test:\'a0
\f1 if a change alters outputs for identical pinned inputs (workflow digest + model hash), it's a contract break; if it only changes speed, resources, or error text, it's a compatible bump.
\f0 \
Conformance suite per capability: golden input/output fixtures, schema round-trip, error-category mapping, availability-probe truthfulness (break a prerequisite \uc0\u8594  capability must hide), and a leakage test asserting public errors stay within the five categories. Deliberately stop there \'97 the registry is code and conformance is CI; that is the whole extensibility mechanism, and resisting a plugin ABI is the point.\
