\f2\b\fs40 \cf2 \strokec2 7. The orchestrator duplicate-free invariant\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs32 \cf2 Child identity is a pure function of\'a0
\f9\fs28 \cb5 (parent ULID, role, index)
\f0\fs32 \cb3 \'a0\'97 encoded in the key\'a0
\f6\fs28 \cb5 reigh.orch:v1:<parent>:<role>:<index>
\f0\fs32 \cb3 . Given the immutable parent spec, the child multiset is deterministic; therefore any coordinator, at any point of any crash, converges to the same set. Duplicates are impossible provided (a) role/index derive from spec position, never runtime counters or discovery order, and (b) admission is the only path by which children exist.\
The durable facts, all in the one database behind the one writer: immutable parent spec; parent lease/fence; child tasks keyed deterministically; hard dependency edges; child terminal states; admission and completion receipts.\

\f1 Reconstruction algorithm
\f0 \'a0for a fresh coordinator:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Reclaim the parent \uc0\u8594  new attempt, new fence; the old fence invalidates any zombie coordinator's in-flight mutations at the admission and settlement gates.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Compute the planned child set from the spec.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Join against existing children by key: terminal-success satisfies the dependency; nonterminal children are adopted (their own lease lifecycle proceeds independently); terminally failed retryable children get a new attempt on the\'a0
\f5\i same
\f0\i0 \'a0child task, preserving identity under the parent's retry budget.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Admit missing children with their deterministic keys; a lost ack replays into the original receipt.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 All required children succeed \uc0\u8594  fenced, receipted parent completion (replay-safe, so no double completion); any required non-retryable failure \u8594  parent fails; cancellation sweeps nonterminal run members.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 Every effect is either\'a0
\f1 idempotent-by-key or fenced
\f0 \'a0\'97 that conjunction is the formal invariant. Validate it with model-checker-style exhaustive interleaving: inject crashes at each coordinator step \'d7 each kernel response (ack delivered/lost), asserting child set == planned set, parent terminal exactly once, and no orphaned running children after parent termination. Watch one subtle hazard: if fan-out count ever depends on intermediate outputs, derive index from stable content identity, not iteration order.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs40 \cf2 \strokec2 8. The correct local-trust boundary\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf2 Single-user removes tenancy, not adversaries. The realistic set: malicious web pages (DNS rebinding, CSRF against loopback, drive-by port scanning), hostile project inputs (archives, filenames, workflow JSON/YAML, media decoders), other local processes (anything user-level can connect to loopback), and supply chain (models, node packs \'97 which are arbitrary Python).\
Cheap controls, in order:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Binding + Host check:
\f0 \'a0bind 127.0.0.1 and require Host to be the loopback literal \'97 kills DNS rebinding outright.\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Boot token:
\f0 \'a0launcher writes a per-boot secret (0600 file) presented as a header by browser app and worker alike. Kills confused-deputy from other local processes at near-zero cost; this generalizes the existing "receipt secrecy."\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 CSRF:
\f0 \'a0require a custom header on all mutations \'97 forces CORS preflight, which the strict allowlist rejects for foreign origins.\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Path confinement:
\f0 \'a0all file access through the managed-tree resolver; reject absolute paths,\'a0
\f6\fs28 \cb5 ..
\f0\fs32 \cb3 , and symlink escapes; storage keys are hashes, never user filenames; sanitize display names for the UI.\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Parser hardening:
\f0 \'a0strict schemas with size/recursion/alias limits for workflow JSON/YAML (YAML bombs); decode-dimension and size caps before media decode (decompression bombs).\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Workflow/code boundary:
\f0 \'a0digest pinning (already ratified) plus node-type allowlisting \'97 user workflows run only against reviewed node sets, because a Comfy node is arbitrary code.\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Resource limits:
\f0 \'a0body caps, quarantine quotas, concurrent-task caps, log rotation.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 Explicitly rejected as disproportionate: full auth, mTLS, per-request signing. Deliverable: an actor \'d7 vector \'d7 control \'d7 residual-risk table, plus tests \'97 rebinding blocked, cross-origin POST preflight-blocked, path-traversal suite, hostile-archive fuzz corpus, YAML bomb rejected.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

